  "id": "guilty-knowledge-test",
  "term": "guilty knowledge test",
  "definition": "A guilty knowledge test is a method for assessing whether a person recognizes details linked to an event, based on their responses to presented information. In the packet, a P3-based version uses the size of the P3 response as an indicator of how strongly the person recognizes a critical stimulus.",
